{
  "_comment": "Shared parity fixture for resolve_dataset_refs (server: web-app/lambdas/endpoints/dataset_ref.py; CLI mirror: qa_studio_cli/runner/dataset_ref.py). Consumed by test_dataset_ref.py and the CLI parity test. Inputs: `steps` (plain step dicts, resource-API shape) and `datasets` ({dataset_id: {columns, rows}} — the fetcher is `datasets.get`). Expected: either `expected` (exact resolved step list: dataset_id kept, repeat_columns/repeat_rows filled from the dataset, every other step untouched) or `error` ({dataset_id} of the DatasetNotFoundError). `fetched` is the exact sequence of dataset ids the fetcher was called with (each distinct id once, in first-seen step order; empty when nothing references a dataset). Optional precedence block: `overrides` ({repeat label: {columns, rows}}, the --dataset-file layer) and `expanded` (exact output of expand_repeat_steps(resolved, overrides)) — the CLI override wins over the application dataset by label.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "inline repeat is untouched and the fetcher is never called",
      "steps": [
        {"id": "r1", "sort": 1, "step_type": "repeat", "instruction": "Users",
         "repeat_columns": ["email"], "repeat_rows": [["a@x.test"], ["b@x.test"]]},
        {"id": "c1", "sort": 2, "step_type": "navigation", "instruction": "Type {{email}}", "parent_step_id": "r1"},
        {"id": "p1", "sort": 3, "step_type": "validation", "instruction": "Done"}
      ],
      "datasets": {"ds-1": {"columns": ["email"], "rows": [["ignored"]]}},
      "expected": [
        {"id": "r1", "sort": 1, "step_type": "repeat", "instruction": "Users",
         "repeat_columns": ["email"], "repeat_rows": [["a@x.test"], ["b@x.test"]]},
        {"id": "c1", "sort": 2, "step_type": "navigation", "instruction": "Type {{email}}", "parent_step_id": "r1"},
        {"id": "p1", "sort": 3, "step_type": "validation", "instruction": "Done"}
      ],
      "fetched": []
    },
    {
